From: SweetAdreno bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] gauguin: SQE dbg ph0/ph1 self-parse boot-arg

v242 verdict prep: the 0281 ph0/ph1 trigger at the submit entry
tested gg_imem_opt before the gg_ib_sanitize armed point parsed
gauguinimem, so both entry dumps never fired (v242 log line 8480
arms after submit #1 and inside submit #2). ph2 (the v241 point)
fired normally and its tag array matched v241 bit-for-bit (122
filled / 27 space-1 / 6 inv), proving the ROM restore image is
deterministic across boots. 0282 makes the trigger block parse
the boot-arg itself (static local, -2 sentinel) instead of
depending on the armed ordering.

---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/gauguin_gpu.c b/bsd/dev/gauguin_gpu.c
--- a/bsd/dev/gauguin_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/gauguin_gpu.c
@@ -8753,10 +8753,24 @@ gauguin_cp_submit(const uint64_t * addresses, const uint32_t * words, uint32_t c
 	 * after submit 0 completed. ph2 (the v241 point) samples after the
 	 * ME consumed ring work. Restore image present at ph0 -> boot-time
 	 * load; appears only by ph2 -> ME-execution driven.
+	 * 0282: parse the boot-arg here instead of relying on the
+	 * gg_ib_sanitize armed point - v242 showed that point arms only
+	 * after the first submit entry (and inside submit #2), so the
+	 * 0281 check on gg_imem_opt never fired at ph0/ph1.
 	 */
-	if (gg_imem_opt >= 0 && gg_submit_seen < 2) {
-		gg_sqe_dump(gg_submit_seen);
-		gg_submit_seen++;
+	{
+		static int ph_en = -2;
+		int v = -1;
+
+		if (ph_en == -2) {
+			(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("gauguinimem", &v,
+			    sizeof(v));
+			ph_en = v;
+		}
+		if (ph_en >= 0 && gg_submit_seen < 2) {
+			gg_sqe_dump(gg_submit_seen);
+			gg_submit_seen++;
+		}
 	}
 	need = 4u * count + 13u;	/* + 2 invalidates, + scratch, + RB_CCU_CNTL */
 	if (gg_wai_opt < 0) {
